  "detail": {
    "longDescription": "I've been trying to figure out how to use ImageData and Canvases to make images by changing the individual pixels, yet the canvas remains blank despite code looking almost identical to other examples. I tested example code, and it did work, so it's the problem is definitely something with this code in particular. <!DOCTYPE html> <html> <canvas id=\"canvas\" width=\"100\" height=\"100\" style=\"border:1px solid #000\"></canvas> <br> <button onclick=\"testFunction()\"> Test </button> </html> <script type=\"text/javascript\"> function testFunction() { var canvas = document.getElementById(\"canvas\"); var ctx = canvas.getContext(\"2d\"); var imgData = ctx.createImageData(100, 100); for (let i = 0; i < imgData.data.length; i+=4) { if (i%2 == 0) { imgData.data[i] = 255; } else { imgData.data[i] = 0; imgData.data[i+1] = 0; imgData.data[i+2] = 0; } } ctx.putImageData(imgData,0,0); } </script>",
